  "question": "求 $\\int_0^{x^1 - 1}\\max \\{1, t^2\\} \\mathrm{d}t, x \\in (-\\infty, +\\infty)$ .",
  "answer": "$$ \\int_ {0} ^ {x ^ {3} - 1} \\max \\{1, t ^ {2} \\} d t = \\left\\{ \\begin{array}{l l} - \\frac {2}{3} + \\frac {1}{3} (x ^ {3} - 1) ^ {3}, & x < 0, \\\\ x ^ {3} - 1, & 0 \\leqslant x \\leqslant \\sqrt [ 3 ]{2}, \\\\ \\frac {2}{3} + \\frac {1}{3} (x ^ {3} - 1) ^ {3}, & x > \\sqrt [ 3 ]{2}. \\end{array} \\right. $$",
  "ref_source": "textbook:puheping_math_contest_v2",
